{"id":"G0652","lemma":"ἀπόστολος","transliteration":"apostolos","sayIt":"apostolos","language":"Greek","partOfSpeech":"noun, masculine","gloss":"apostle","meaning":"ἀπόστολος, -ου, ὁ\n(ἀοστέλλω), [in LXX; 3Ki.14:6 A (שָׁלַח) * ;]\n1. a fleet, an expedition (Dem.).\n2. a messenger, one sent on a mission (Hdt., LXX, l.with, and π.; see M, Pr., 37 f.; MM, see word; M, Th., i, 2:7 and reff.): Jhn.13:16, 2Co.8:23 Php.2:25.\n3. In NT, an Apostle of Christ\n(a) with special ref. to the Twelve: Mat.10:2, Mrk.3:14, Luk.11:49, Eph.3:5, Rev.18:20, al., equality with whom is claimed by St. Paul, Gal.1:1, 11 ff, 1Ti.2:7, a1.;\n(b) in a wider sense of prominent Christian teachers, as Barnabas, Act.14:14, apparently also Silvanus and Timothy, 1Th.2:6, and perhaps Andronicus and Junias (Junia?), Rom.16:7 (see ICC, in l); of false teachers, claiming apostleship: 2Co.11:5 11:13, Rev.2:2. (On the different uses of the term in NT, see Lit., Gal., 92-101; Cremer, 530; DB, i, 126; DCG, i, 105; Enc. Br., ii, 196 ff.)\n(AS)","glosses":["apostles","apostle","messenger","super-apostles","other apostles","elders"],"count":78,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"mat-10","v":2,"renderings":{"bsb":"apostles","kjv":"apostles"}},{"chapterId":"mrk-3","v":14,"renderings":{}},{"chapterId":"mrk-6","v":30,"renderings":{"bsb":"apostles","kjv":"the apostles"}},{"chapterId":"luk-6","v":13,"renderings":{"bsb":"apostles"}},{"chapterId":"luk-9","v":10,"renderings":{"bsb":"apostles","kjv":"the apostles"}},{"chapterId":"luk-11","v":49,"renderings":{"bsb":"apostles","kjv":"apostles"}},{"chapterId":"luk-17","v":5,"renderings":{"bsb":"apostles","kjv":"the apostles"}},{"chapterId":"luk-22","v":14,"renderings":{"bsb":"apostles","kjv":"apostles"}},{"chapterId":"luk-24","v":10,"renderings":{"bsb":"apostles"}},{"chapterId":"jhn-13","v":16,"renderings":{"bsb":"a messenger","kjv":"he that is sent"}},{"chapterId":"act-1","v":2,"renderings":{"bsb":"apostles","kjv":"unto the apostles"}},{"chapterId":"act-1","v":26,"renderings":{"b